I fixed #1043 and committed it as 1ffeeb41. After a /cd, /context now marks a fence-blocked instruction file as refused instead of listing it with a line count. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings, and the fmt check all pass.

What changed
• `src/context.rs`: There is now one fenced loop, list_project_context_files_fenced(dir, restrictions, cd_deny, cd_allow). Before reading each file, it asks the same check the loader uses (path_guard_refusal_lists, only for files that exist) and returns both the listed and the refused files. list_project_context_files now takes the session's startup fence and the /cd lists and calls that loop. The old bare-read loop is gone, and the lister prints no warning because the loader already does.
• `/context`: a refused file shows as NAME (refused by the directory fence: REASON). The reason is cleaned with sanitize_for_display and the line uses no special symbols.
• `/doctor`: it now gets the session's fence passed through handle_doctor/run_doctor_checks, and lists only files the loader would accept.
• Wiring: dispatch.rs passes the session's directory restrictions to both commands. Shell yoyo doctor (dispatch_sub.rs) has no session, so it passes an empty fence.

Tests (in src/context_fence_tests.rs, using local /cd lists rather than the process-wide ones):
• The loader and the lister agree on the same /cd-deny fixture: both refuse CLAUDE.md, and it is not in the listed files.
• A neighbouring AGENTS.md outside the denied dir is still listed with its line count.
• A startup deny refuses the file in the lister too.
• With no fence, the output equals the old bare-read loop exactly.
• The refused line strips escape codes and uses no special symbols.

I also checked that the tests catch the bug: removing the check from the lister made exactly the two refusal tests fail, and every other test stayed green. I restored the check in the same command.

Left out of this fix, filed as #1045:
• /doctor leaves a refused file out of its list without saying so. If every instruction file is refused, it wrongly says to create a YOYO.md.
• Shell yoyo doctor doesn't check a [directories] deny at all, so it can list a file a real session would refuse.

Size: src/context.rs is now 2020 lines. That is over the 2000-line cap but inside the 50-line grace band, so the size test warns rather than fails.

Beyond the task's file list: I added a short note to docs/src/configuration/permissions.md and an entry to ARCHITECTURE.md. That entry marks the #1042 entry's "still reads unfenced" sentence as no longer true.
